277 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (For the Segmentation task, only benign and malignant images were used, this reduced the dataset to 697 images, making generalization more challenging due to the limited data. In a real-world setting, using a pre-trained network would be a more effective approach; however, for the purposes of this project, we chose to train the model from scratch to evaluate its capabilities.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
278 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (First of all we apply transformations to the images, using Data Augmentation Techniques, to ensure consistency and increase model generalizability. Then, we create a custom SegmentationDataset to ensure that each ultrasound image is correctly paired with its corresponding mask, this guarantees reliable data loading and prevents errors during training and evaluation. We also do a visual inspection of the samples of the segmentation dataset, in this way we verify that the image and mask are correctly aligned.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
